---
# A lost prompt leaves nothing to do but look at it: that is rest, not a
# deadlock (and it is what ARowResolves below is about).
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Stop pressed in another tab (its Stop button or the palette's "Stop
# this turn") while this tab's prompt is still on its way to a session
# that has no child. stop_interrupt.fizz is one tab, where the page's
# own Stop first awaits its in-flight sends; here the Stop comes from a
# tab whose inflight set is empty, so nothing orders it after the send.
#
# Tab A sends to a session whose child is gone (the previous turn was
# stopped: a SIGINT ends a headless child). Supervisor.Send
# (internal/serve/supervisor.go) is one HTTP request in two steps:
#   ensure    spawns a child and reserves the lease (s.kids[id] = ch),
#             then start() returns with cmd and stdin set;
#   writePrompt  sets ch.unread, then writes the line; 200 or an error.
# Supervisor.Interrupt holds only when `ch.unread && !ch.inTurn`. Between
# ensure and writePrompt unread is still false, so an Interrupt there
# SIGINTs the fresh child at once.
#
# Tab B can press Stop only while it believes the turn is live: its
# composer's `live` is row.status === "running" (B has no send of its
# own) and the palette's "Stop this turn" shows on the same condition.
# While A's prompt is unread the server's row is not running (no input
# recorded yet), so B reaches the gap only with a stale row: its list
# poll is 4 s (12 s while it streams). Init is that: the previous turn
# was running when B last polled; it was stopped, its child exited, and
# B has not polled since.
#
# Corrections to the mapped model (the code wins):
#   - EnsureDone and MarkUnread are one step (WriteA). Between ensure
#     returning and writePrompt setting unread there is only the
#     background-agent `running` slot, which no Interrupt reads; for
#     Interrupt the whole ensure..writePrompt span is "started, unread
#     false", the state phase == "ensuring" stands for.
#   - "HoldExpires" and "ChildExits" are kept, and "ChildTakes" is Take.
#     A SIGINT is delivered to a started process at once; what the model
#     orders is when the child dies of it (ChildSignal). A child with a
#     SIGINT on its way never takes its prompt: booting, it dies of it;
#     booted and idle, headless exits 0 on it.
#   - SwallowTimerA cannot fire in this flow and is left out. Thread's
#     swallowedByStop needs (1) the row's id in stoppedIds, which only
#     that tab's own Stop fills, and (2) a done or cancelled recorded
#     after the row. A prompt killed unread records neither: the child
#     dies before it writes anything. So the rescue misses a lost prompt
#     even when A itself pressed Stop, and whichever tab pressed it.
#   - The stale holdGen timer (stop_interrupt.fizz) is not modelled:
#     every release here is followed by the child's exit, and a timer
#     that outlives its child finds ch.dropped and does nothing.
#   - The turn is never replied to or finished here: this flow ends at
#     the Stop, and "stopped before any reply" is what makes the
#     restore reachable. turn_lifecycle and stop_interrupt cover the rest.
#
# Fields (Session role):
#   phase    the lease: "none" (no child) | "ensuring" (spawned, prompt
#            not yet written: unread false) | "unread" (written, not
#            taken) | "turn" (taken, the turn runs)
#   status   server row: "stopped" (the previous turn, or this one
#            cancelled) | "running" (open turn and a live child)
#   taken    A's prompt became a turn (its input is recorded)
#   held     an interrupt is held (ch.held); timer: its 20 s timer pends
#   sigint   a SIGINT the child has not yet died of: "" | "early" (sent
#            in the ensure gap) | "sent" (to a running turn, or a hold
#            released by the take) | "expired" (released by holdLimit)
#   arow     tab A's pending row: "" | "sending" (request in flight) |
#            "accepted" (200, not landed: "Sending…") | "landed" |
#            "failed" (the error row with Retry)
#   bview    tab B's row says running (stale or fresh)
#   bstop    tab B's thread stop state: "" | "stopping" | "failed"
#   brestore tab B's restoreOnStop ref (set by its thread Stop only)
#   bpal     tab B's palette Stop was posted while B's row says running
#   bdraft   "" | "restored": a stopped prompt put back in B's composer

role Session:
    action Init:
        self.phase = "none"
        self.status = "stopped"
        self.taken = False
        self.held = False
        self.timer = False
        self.sigint = ""
        self.arow = ""
        self.bview = True
        self.bstop = ""
        self.brestore = False
        self.bpal = False
        self.bdraft = ""

    # POST /api/sessions/{id}/interrupt, from any tab. False is the 404
    # (no child holds the lease).
    atomic func interrupt():
        if self.phase == "none":
            return False
        if self.phase == "ensuring":
            # started(), unread false: SIGINT now.
            if self.sigint == "":
                self.sigint = "early"
        elif self.phase == "unread":
            # unread && !inTurn: hold; a repeat Stop arms another timer
            # of the same generation.
            self.held = True
            self.timer = True
        elif self.sigint == "":
            self.sigint = "sent"
        return True

    # Tab A sends while its row is idle; Send's ensure spawns a child.
    atomic action SendA:
        require self.arow == "" and self.phase == "none"
        self.phase = "ensuring"
        self.arow = "sending"

    # writePrompt: unread, then the write. A child already dead of an
    # early SIGINT has no reader on its stdin: EPIPE, a 500, and A shows
    # the failure. A child with the SIGINT still on its way takes the
    # line into its pipe: 200, "Sending…".
    atomic fair action WriteA:
        require self.arow == "sending"
        if self.phase == "none":
            self.arow = "failed"
        else:
            self.phase = "unread"
            self.arow = "accepted"

    # The child's first output: unread clears, a held interrupt is
    # released into the turn it can now cancel.
    atomic fair action Take:
        require self.phase == "unread" and self.sigint == ""
        self.phase = "turn"
        self.status = "running"
        self.taken = True
        self.timer = False
        if self.held:
            self.held = False
            self.sigint = "sent"

    # holdLimit passed with the prompt unread: the hold is released as a
    # SIGINT to a child with nothing to cancel.
    atomic fair action HoldExpires:
        require self.timer
        self.timer = False
        self.held = False
        if self.sigint == "":
            self.sigint = "expired"

    # The child dies of the SIGINT. Mid-turn it records cancelled (then
    # the bookkeeping done) and exits: the row reads stopped. Before the
    # take it exits with nothing recorded, and the unread line dies with
    # it. drop() hands the lease back; a pending timer finds it dropped.
    atomic fair action ChildSignal:
        require self.sigint != "" and self.phase != "none"
        if self.phase == "turn":
            self.status = "stopped"
        self.phase = "none"
        self.sigint = ""
        self.held = False
        self.timer = False

    # A's transcript shows the input: the row lands.
    atomic fair action PollA:
        require self.arow == "accepted" and self.taken
        self.arow = "landed"

    # B's thread Stop (button or Esc): stopping, restoreOnStop, and B's
    # inflight wait, which is empty, then the POST.
    atomic action StopB:
        require self.bview and self.bstop != "stopping"
        self.bstop = "stopping"
        self.brestore = True
        ok = self.interrupt()
        if not ok:
            self.bstop = "failed"

    # The palette's "Stop this turn" in tab B: act(() => api.interrupt())
    # and nothing else. A 404 is act's toast.
    atomic action PaletteStopB:
        require self.bview
        ok = self.interrupt()
        self.bpal = True

    # B's list poll brings its row up to date. Once B's row is not live
    # the Thread's effects run: stopping clears, and restoreOnStop puts
    # a prompt stopped before any reply into the (empty) draft.
    atomic fair action PollB:
        require self.bview != (self.status == "running")
        self.bview = self.status == "running"
        if not self.bview:
            self.bstop = ""
            self.bpal = False
            if self.brestore and self.taken and self.status == "stopped" and self.bdraft == "":
                self.brestore = False
                self.bdraft = "restored"

action Init:
    session = Session()

# Once writePrompt has marked the prompt unread, no Stop from any tab
# reaches the child before it takes it: a Stop is held, and the only
# SIGINT that reaches an unread prompt is the one holdLimit released
# (or one sent in the ensure gap, before unread existed).
always assertion HoldCoversUnread:
    return not (session.sigint == "sent" and session.phase == "unread")

# A hold lives only while its prompt is unread, and its timer only with it.
always assertion HoldOnlyWhileUnread:
    return (not session.held or session.phase == "unread") and (session.timer == session.held)

# The server's row says running only while a child runs the turn.
always assertion RunningHasAChild:
    return session.status != "running" or session.phase == "turn"

# A's row lands only on a recorded input, and fails only when the child
# died before the write: a failed row's prompt never ran.
always assertion RowMatchesTranscript:
    return (session.arow != "landed" or session.taken) and (session.arow != "failed" or not session.taken)

# Only B's own thread Stop restores, and only a prompt that was taken.
always assertion RestoreOnlyAfterThreadStop:
    return session.bdraft == "" or (session.taken and session.status == "stopped")

# A held interrupt is released: by the take, or by holdLimit.
always eventually assertion HoldReleased:
    return not session.held

# B's "Stopping" clears without a reload, whatever the Stop hit.
always eventually assertion BStoppingClears:
    return session.bstop != "stopping"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claims the code does NOT meet. Each was checked by adding it to this
# spec: fizz fails it with the trace given. They are findings, left out
# so the check stays green; the product is not changed in this stage.
#
# EnsureGapHeld (mapped: "an interrupt between ensure and writePrompt's
# unread is held"):
#     always assertion EnsureGapHeld:
#         return session.sigint != "early"
#   FAILED: SendA, StopB -> sigint "early". Interrupt SIGINTs the child
#   Send just spawned, because unread is set only in writePrompt.
#
# ARowResolves (mapped liveness: "tab A's Sending… row resolves without
# a reload", and "every tab's pending row eventually fails or
# re-queues, whichever tab pressed Stop"):
#     always eventually assertion ARowResolves:
#         return session.arow != "sending" and session.arow != "accepted"
#   FAILED: SendA, StopB (early SIGINT), WriteA (200 into the dying
#   child's pipe), ChildSignal: arow "accepted" forever. A second way:
#   SendA, WriteA, StopB (held), HoldExpires, ChildSignal: the same.
#   Neither records a done or cancelled, and A never pressed Stop, so
#   swallowedByStop has nothing to go on.
#
# PaletteStopLikeThreadStop (mapped: "palette Stop behaves like the
# thread's Stop: inflight wait, stopping state, restore"):
#     always assertion PaletteStopLikeThreadStop:
#         return not (session.bpal and session.bstop != "stopping")
#   FAILED: PaletteStopB (from Init) -> bpal with bstop "". The palette
#   posts api.interrupt directly: B's Stop button stays enabled, no
#   "Stopping", no restoreOnStop (so a turn stopped from the palette
#   never gives its prompt back), and in the sending tab itself it
#   would skip the inflight await that orders Stop after the send.
